/Title (The most known achievement is the CRISPR which consists in modifying specific points in the DNA. This powerful tool has been used for the creation of Casgevy therapy for sickle cell anemia and connects the first personalized therapy for a baby with a rare genetic disease. Global organizations like the World Health Organization \(WHO\), UNESCO, along with health agencies like the FDA, and EMA, are working to create shared rules. Key debates focus on allowing gene edits in regular body cells while banning edits passed to future generations, protecting patient privacy, and ensuring fair access for developing countries.)
